{"v":15,"id":"e20","kid":"emma","title":"Why Sleep Matters for Teenagers","zh":"为什么睡眠对青少年很重要","level":"B1","genre":"科普 · 健康","src":"facts","sum":"13-18 岁的青少年每晚需要 8-10 小时睡眠。睡觉时身体在修复、大脑在整理记忆；睡眠不足会让人注意力差、脾气坏。文章最后给出改善睡眠的建议。","words":310,"paras":[{"t":"Do you find it hard to get up in the morning? Do you sometimes feel sleepy in class? If so, you are not alone. Many teenagers around the world do not get enough sleep.","w":[[0,2,"do",-1],[3,6,"you",-1],[7,11,"find",-1],[12,14,"it",-1],[15,19,"hard",-1],[20,22,"to",-1],[23,26,"get",0],[27,29,"up",0],[30,32,"in",-1],[33,36,"the",-1],[37,44,"morning",-1],[46,48,"do",-1],[49,52,"you",-1],[53,62,"sometimes",-1],[63,67,"feel",-1],[68,74,"sleepy",-1],[75,77,"in",-1],[78,83,"class",-1],[85,87,"if",1],[88,90,"so",1],[92,95,"you",-1],[96,99,"are",-1],[100,103,"not",2],[104,109,"alone",2],[111,115,"many",-1],[116,125,"teenagers",-1],[126,132,"around",-1],[133,136,"the",-1],[137,142,"world",-1],[143,145,"do",-1],[146,149,"not",-1],[150,153,"get",16],[154,160,"enough",16],[161,166,"sleep",16]]},{"t":"Doctors say that children aged 6 to 12 need 9 to 12 hours of sleep each night, and teenagers aged 13 to 18 need 8 to 10 hours. However, studies show that many teenagers sleep only about seven hours on school nights, and some sleep even less.","w":[[0,7,"doctors",-1],[8,11,"say",-1],[12,16,"that",-1],[17,25,"children",-1],[26,30,"aged",-1],[33,35,"to",-1],[39,43,"need",-1],[46,48,"to",-1],[52,57,"hours",-1],[58,60,"of",-1],[61,66,"sleep",-1],[67,71,"each",-1],[72,77,"night",-1],[79,82,"and",-1],[83,92,"teenagers",-1],[93,97,"aged",-1],[101,103,"to",-1],[107,111,"need",-1],[114,116,"to",-1],[120,125,"hours",-1],[127,134,"however",-1],[136,143,"studies",-1],[144,148,"show",-1],[149,153,"that",-1],[154,158,"many",-1],[159,168,"teenagers",-1],[169,174,"sleep",-1],[175,179,"only",-1],[180,185,"about",-1],[186,191,"seven",-1],[192,197,"hours",-1],[198,200,"on",-1],[201,207,"school",3],[208,214,"nights",3],[216,219,"and",-1],[220,224,"some",-1],[225,230,"sleep",-1],[231,235,"even",-1],[236,240,"less",-1]]},{"t":"Why is sleep so important? While you sleep, your body is busy. It repairs your muscles, helps you grow and makes your body better at fighting illness. Your brain is busy, too. It sorts through what you learned during the day and stores the important information. That is why a good night's sleep before a test can be more useful than studying until midnight.","w":[[0,3,"why",-1],[4,6,"is",-1],[7,12,"sleep",-1],[13,15,"so",-1],[16,25,"important",-1],[27,32,"while",-1],[33,36,"you",-1],[37,42,"sleep",-1],[44,48,"your",-1],[49,53,"body",-1],[54,56,"is",-1],[57,61,"busy",-1],[63,65,"it",-1],[66,73,"repairs",-1],[74,78,"your",-1],[79,86,"muscles",-1],[88,93,"helps",-1],[94,97,"you",-1],[98,102,"grow",-1],[103,106,"and",-1],[107,112,"makes",-1],[113,117,"your",-1],[118,122,"body",-1],[123,129,"better",17],[130,132,"at",17],[133,141,"fighting",-1],[142,149,"illness",-1],[151,155,"your",-1],[156,161,"brain",-1],[162,164,"is",-1],[165,169,"busy",-1],[171,174,"too",-1],[176,178,"it",-1],[179,184,"sorts",4],[185,192,"through",4],[193,197,"what",-1],[198,201,"you",-1],[202,209,"learned",-1],[210,216,"during",-1],[217,220,"the",-1],[221,224,"day",-1],[225,228,"and",-1],[229,235,"stores",-1],[236,239,"the",-1],[240,249,"important",-1],[250,261,"information",-1],[263,267,"that",5],[268,270,"is",5],[271,274,"why",5],[275,276,"a",6],[277,281,"good",6],[282,289,"night's",6],[290,295,"sleep",6],[296,302,"before",-1],[303,304,"a",-1],[305,309,"test",-1],[310,313,"can",-1],[314,316,"be",-1],[317,321,"more",-1],[322,328,"useful",-1],[329,333,"than",-1],[334,342,"studying",-1],[343,348,"until",-1],[349,357,"midnight",-1]]},{"t":"When people do not get enough sleep, they often have trouble paying attention. They may feel grumpy, make more mistakes and react more slowly. This can be dangerous when you are riding a bike or crossing a busy street.","w":[[0,4,"when",-1],[5,11,"people",-1],[12,14,"do",-1],[15,18,"not",-1],[19,22,"get",16],[23,29,"enough",16],[30,35,"sleep",16],[37,41,"they",-1],[42,47,"often",-1],[48,52,"have",7],[53,60,"trouble",7],[61,67,"paying",8],[68,77,"attention",8],[79,83,"they",-1],[84,87,"may",-1],[88,92,"feel",-1],[93,99,"grumpy",-1],[101,105,"make",-1],[106,110,"more",-1],[111,119,"mistakes",-1],[120,123,"and",-1],[124,129,"react",-1],[130,134,"more",-1],[135,141,"slowly",-1],[143,147,"this",-1],[148,151,"can",-1],[152,154,"be",-1],[155,164,"dangerous",-1],[165,169,"when",-1],[170,173,"you",-1],[174,177,"are",-1],[178,184,"riding",-1],[185,186,"a",-1],[187,191,"bike",-1],[192,194,"or",-1],[195,203,"crossing",-1],[204,205,"a",-1],[206,210,"busy",-1],[211,217,"street",-1]]},{"t":"Teenagers have a special problem. During the teenage years, the body clock changes, and many teens naturally feel sleepy later at night. But school still starts early in the morning. Phones make the problem worse. Their bright screens tell the brain that it is still daytime, and games and messages keep the mind active.","w":[[0,9,"teenagers",-1],[10,14,"have",-1],[15,16,"a",-1],[17,24,"special",-1],[25,32,"problem",-1],[34,40,"during",-1],[41,44,"the",-1],[45,52,"teenage",-1],[53,58,"years",-1],[60,63,"the",-1],[64,68,"body",9],[69,74,"clock",9],[75,82,"changes",-1],[84,87,"and",-1],[88,92,"many",-1],[93,98,"teens",-1],[99,108,"naturally",-1],[109,113,"feel",-1],[114,120,"sleepy",-1],[121,126,"later",-1],[127,129,"at",-1],[130,135,"night",-1],[137,140,"but",-1],[141,147,"school",-1],[148,153,"still",-1],[154,160,"starts",-1],[161,166,"early",-1],[167,169,"in",-1],[170,173,"the",-1],[174,181,"morning",-1],[183,189,"phones",-1],[190,194,"make",10],[195,198,"the",10],[199,206,"problem",10],[207,212,"worse",10],[214,219,"their",-1],[220,226,"bright",-1],[227,234,"screens",-1],[235,239,"tell",-1],[240,243,"the",-1],[244,249,"brain",-1],[250,254,"that",-1],[255,257,"it",-1],[258,260,"is",-1],[261,266,"still",-1],[267,274,"daytime",-1],[276,279,"and",-1],[280,285,"games",-1],[286,289,"and",-1],[